  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticsalah.com/ontology/RukuPosture">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Ne1078a89be7b4c4081fd64141a46ef24"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticsalah.com/ontology/Posture"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">In prayer, it refers to the bowing at the waist from standing (qiyām) on the completion of recitation (qiraʾat) of a portion of the Qur'an in Islamic formal prayers (salah). There is a consensus on the obligatory nature of the rukūʿ. The position of rukūʿ is established by bending over till the hands are on the knees and remaining in that position until one attains a relaxed state while glorifying God (سُبْحَانَ رَبِّيَ الْعَظِيم subḥāna rabbiya l-ʿaẓīm, "Glory be to my Lord, the Most Magnificent!") thrice or more in odd number of times.</dcterms:description>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ruku</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="ar">رُكوع</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="ur">رُكوع</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:seeAlso>https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1816496</rdfs:seeAlso>
    <owl:sameAs xml:lang="en">http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ruku</owl:sameAs>
  </rdf:Description>
