  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticsalah.com/ontology/Isha">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticsalah.com/ontology/SalahType"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticsalah.com/ontology/ObligatorySalah"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="kashmiri">Khoftan Nemaz</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="ar">صلاة العشاء</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="punjabi">Khuftaan di namaz</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Isha Prayer</rdfs:label>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Night Prayer</skos:altLabel>
    <owl:sameAs xml:lang="en">http://dbpedia.org/resource/Isha_prayer</owl:sameAs>
    <owl:sameAs>https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q757365</owl:sameAs>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">The Isha prayer (Arabic: صلاة العشاء ṣalāt al-ʿišāʾ, "night prayer") is one of the five mandatory salah (Islamic prayer)
It is a four rak'ah prayer in Sunni Islam. The two Sunnah rak'ah following the Isha' are highly recommended and so is the three rakat Witr. There are a few optional prayers that can be recited after the Isha' prayer, including the Nafilat ul-Layl prayers (together termed tahajjud), as well as the tarawih in Ramadan.</dcterms:description>
  </rdf:Description>
